  ('30545530146286955', 'The Passion of Darkly Noon', 1995, 'Mystery, Drama, Thriller, Horror', 'Philip Ridley, John de Borman', 'Philip Ridley', 'Brendan Fraser, Ashley Judd, Viggo Mortensen, Lou Myers, Loren Dean, Grace Zabriskie, Kate Harper, Mel Cobb', 'R', 'Desire torments a former cultist taking refuge at the home of a scantily clad woman whose husband is away.', 'Desire torments a former cultist taking refuge at the home of a scantily clad woman whose husband is away.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/nx459fssgbvYTBcL5CC0lH1gbwq.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:37062'),
  ('389588766721986260', 'The Passion of Martin', 1991, 'Comedy', 'Alexander Payne, David Rudd', 'Ernesto Sábato', 'Charley Hayward, Lisa Zane, Lauren Tuerk, Holgie Forrester', null, 'A lonely photographer gradually develops a rather unhealthy obsession with a young woman he once met by sheer chance.', 'A lonely photographer gradually develops a rather unhealthy obsession with a young woman he once met by sheer chance.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/bMcei3OWI5h7o99NutHRpbxFjrf.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:359116'),
  ('889539320091542985', 'The Passion of Slow Fire', 1961, 'Mystery, Crime, Drama', 'Édouard Molinaro, Jean-Louis Picavet, Sophie Becker', 'Édouard Molinaro, Jean Anouilh, Pierre Kast', 'Jean Desailly, Alexandra Stewart, Monique Mélinand, Yvette Etiévant, Jacques Monod, Marc Cassot, Jacques Pierre, Yves Robert', null, 'Stéphane Blanchon lives a quiet life in Switzerland with his wife, Christine, until a young American boarder named Belle, who was living with them, is found murdered. Despite Stéphane''s innocence, the evidence points to him, and he learns that Belle harbored romantic feelings for him. Suspicions mount against him; even Christine thinks he is the culprit. Stéphane''s sanity begins to crumble, and he lashes out in unprecedented ways.', 'Stéphane Blanchon lives a quiet life in Switzerland with his wife, Christine, until a young American boarder named Belle, who was living with them, is found murdered. Despite Stéphane''s innocence, the evidence points to him, and he learns that Belle harbored romantic feelings for him. Suspicions mount against him; even Christine thinks he is the culprit. Stéphane''s sanity begins to crumble, and he lashes out in unprecedented ways.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/nhBuiiyjzkEpRuCrGFFMpHWW3Wc.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:251967'),
